# PTPX 2026

<small>Warm-up before Genuary: a softbody take on my postcard design for the plotter postcard exchange (#ptpx).</small>

<VideoLoop src="/00/loop.mp4" poster="/00/poster.jpg" label="Softbody shapes from the PTPX postcard SVG, wobbling on a vibrant gradient" />

The postcard design is an SVG. Every closed contour in it is sampled into a ring
of tiny circles connected by spring joints — a soft body simulated with
[JBox2D](https://github.com/jbox2d/jbox2d). On top of that, random lines are shot
across the scene; wherever a line enters and exits the shapes, extra springs are
created, tying the composition together with the white connection lines you see.
There is no gravity, only tiny random impulses, so the whole postcard just...
breathes. The background is a shader interpolating a handful of gradient points
in saturated print-adjacent colors, and the four heavy white frames are the A6
quadrants used for plotting.

```kotlin
// shoot random lines across the scene; where a line crosses the shapes,
// pair up the intersections and connect them with springs
for (lineAttempt in 0 until settings.numConnectionLines * 2) {
    if (jointsCreated >= settings.maxInterShapeJoints) break
    val angle = Random.nextDouble(0.0, PI * 2.0)
    // ... find intersections with every softbody edge ...
    if (intersections.size % 2 != 0) continue
    intersections.sortBy { (it.point - lineStart).length }
    for (pairIdx in 0 until intersections.size / 2) {
        val joint = createSpringJoint(world, body1, body2,
            frequency = settings.interShapeFrequency.toFloat(),
            damping = settings.interShapeDamping.toFloat())
    }
}
```

<SourceLink file="genuary/00PTPX2026.kt" />

Made with [OPENRNDR](https://openrndr.org). The clip on this page is the scripted
render variant (`render/Render00Ptpx.kt`), recorded with orx ScreenRecorder.
